 ## Launch decisions — 2026-10-10
 
 Game's Estimator quest reads a saved, offered service's price range; Marketing reads a saved GBP/review link or a tenant-scoped connected social account. No completion or XP rows are fabricated. Billing uses /api/payments/tenants/:id/billing with owner/admin POST actions own and stop-hosting, plus the existing switch/cancel/portal paths. Same-cadence upgrades settle a guarded prorated difference; downgrades start next renewal. Ownership costs $1,500 with no paid-rent credit. Connected owner hosting is $50/month at the confirmed next paid cycle. If no future paid cycle exists, scheduling stays Pending instead of charging immediately. Live Stripe keys remain rejected; see docs/build-evidence/LAUNCH-DECISIONS/README.md.
+
+
+### Ownership pay-over-time checkout — local test mode
+
+Ownership checkout uses a separate Stripe payment-method configuration containing only card, Klarna and Affirm. Other Checkout purchases use a validated card-only configuration; owner-hosting subscriptions are explicitly card-only. Runtime configuration names are STRIPE_CARD_PAYMENT_METHOD_CONFIGURATION and STRIPE_OWNERSHIP_PAYMENT_METHOD_CONFIGURATION (Dashboard pmc_ IDs, not secrets). Missing configuration reports Not connected; an inactive/live or unexpected-method configuration is rejected. Joe must enable Klarna and Affirm in Stripe Dashboard Settings > Payment methods before go-live. Billing displays official Stripe-sourced marks with approval-qualified text, without a financing amount or APR. Signed paid checkout.session.completed or checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded events settle ownership; pending/failed sessions do not. No provider calls were made. Evidence: ../build-evidence/LAUNCH-DECISIONS/financing/README.md.
